; liblogos_lez_rln_module — the LEZ RLN registry provider. The contract is the
; surface its two consumers use: the membership module's registry provider
; (register_member / get_membership / get_registry_bounds — see
; logos-rln-module/rust-lib/deps/) and anything that
; needs to know whether the module can afford to register (wallet_status /
; get_native_balance). Identity and credential generation belong to the
; membership module, which keeps the secret in-module; this module never
; handles secrets.
; v2.0.0 dropped the C++-era wire freeze: generate_identity,
; compute_rate_commitment, is_member_registered, mint_tokens, the two
; start_*_broadcast methods and the valid_roots / merkle_proof events.
; v3.0.0 dropped the lez_core dependency: this module links the LEZ wallet
; crate and owns its own WalletCore, because a host has exactly one lez_core
; wallet handle, no way to close it, and no way to read back the gas limit it
; was opened with — and a registration needs a limit five times the stock
; default. Configuration moved with the wallet: LEZ_RLN_SEQUENCER names the
; chain, LEZ_RLN_PAYER the fee payer, LEZ_RLN_PAYER_KEY its signing key (a
; fee is reserved from a native balance and the payer must sign, so a wallet
; this module creates can sign but never pay for itself).
; v4.0.0 dropped every token. The registry takes the NATIVE asset only, so
; claim_tokens, get_token_balance and create_holding_account are gone with the
; faucet and the holding-account walk they served, and register_member's
; second parameter is the PAYER — one account that signs the tx, pays the
; registry price from its native balance and pays the fee. The arity is
; unchanged on purpose: rln_gifter_module calls this method positionally from
; out of tree, and dropping a parameter would silently shift id_commitment_hex
; into the payer slot.
; v4.1.0 added use_network and the built-in network table; additive —
; positional callers (rln_gifter_module) unaffected. A wallet home with no
; wallet_config.json and no LEZ_RLN_SEQUENCER now waits ("pending") for
; use_network instead of failing; LEZ_RLN_NETWORK names a table network at
; start-up. Precedence: an existing home config > LEZ_RLN_SEQUENCER (+ optional
; LEZ_RLN_NETWORK label) > LEZ_RLN_NETWORK alone > use_network.
; v4.2.0 added get_fee_state; additive — positional callers unaffected. It is
; what a caller sizes a registration's fee reserve from: the wallet's
; declared max_fee is only a cap, and what the chain actually holds back is
; gas_limit x base fee at the block the tx lands in.
; v4.2.1 adds the testnet network (testnet-z1) to the built-in table; data only.
; v5.1.0 adds check_registry: whether a registry is deployed on the wallet's
; chain, and why not.
; v7.0.0 follows the program off chain for its tree: the registry keeps no
; merkle tree (a zone service builds it from the program's Registered/
; Extended/Slashed/Erased events, and the membership module asks it for
; roots and proofs over libp2p). The config still numbers registrations
; (next_leaf_index, claimed by Register and carried by the Registered event),
; but the membership account does not record its index: get_valid_roots and
; get_merkle_proofs are gone, register_member no longer refuses with
; tree_full, and leaf_index is this module's to answer because it sent the
; registration — each send's claim is recorded (leaf_claims.json in the
; module's persistence dir); register_member replies carry the claim of that
; send, and get_membership answers the latest claim once the membership
; exists (the leaf, since a re-send follows only a send that reverted; absent
; for a membership another sender registered). Configs are the 120-byte
; layout (no merkle_program_id, next_leaf_index appended); a 112- or 144-byte
; config reads as wrong_generation.
; The same release goes back to the lez_core wallet (depends [lez_core]): with
; the tree off chain a Register costs ~52k gas, well inside the shared
; wallet's stock 2M limit, so the bundled wallet_ffi is gone. Nothing on a
; headless node opens lez_core, so this module does: in lez_core's own
; wallet_dir (or LEE_WALLET_HOME_DIR), creating the wallet when there is none,
; and adopting one another consumer already opened if it is on the same
; sequencer (on another chain: wallet_status "failed"). The payer is any
; public account in that wallet with funds — LEZ_RLN_PAYER when it names one
; the wallet holds, else the best-funded, re-picked whenever a payment is
; made; with nothing funded, wallet_status names one account to fund.
; LEZ_RLN_PAYER_KEY is ignored (lez_core cannot import a key). No wallet sync:
; reads and nonces come from the sequencer.
module liblogos_lez_rln_module {
  version "7.0.0"
  description "RLN registry provider (LEZ chain reads + registration/funding txs)"
  category "blockchain"
  depends [lez_core]

  ; Idempotent on-chain registration. Existing membership PDA →
  ; {"already_registered":true}; otherwise submits the Register tx and
  ; returns {"leaf_index":N,"pending":true,"tx_result":s} without waiting for
  ; confirmation; "" on error. leaf_index is this send's claim, which a racing
  ; registration can move (the watcher re-sends with the next): the final
  ; index is get_membership's. already_registered carries leaf_index when
  ; this module sent the registration.
  ; payer_account_id signs the tx, pays rate_limit x price_per_unit of NATIVE
  ; balance to the treasury, and pays the fee — one account, not the
  ; pre-4.0.0 (holding signs, LEZ_RLN_PAYER pays) pair. "" selects the
  ; module's own payer (since 7.0.0: the best-funded account in the lez_core
  ; wallet); a caller paying on someone else's behalf (a gifter) names its
  ; account, whose key that wallet must hold.
  ; Since 5.1.0 a registration the program would refuse is not submitted:
  ; {"error":"<kind>: <reason>"} with kind invalid_commitment (zero, or not a BN254
  ; field element, read little-endian), invalid_rate_limit, registry_full
  ; or insufficient_balance (price + fee reserve at the next base
  ; fee ceiling). "" stays the answer for a config or chain read that failed.
  method register_member(config_account_id: tstr, payer_account_id: tstr, id_commitment_hex: tstr, rate_limit: int) -> tstr

  ; Live NATIVE balance of account_id as a decimal STRING (u128 exceeds JSON
  ; number precision). "" for account_id selects the module's own payer — the
  ; account register_member would charge. {"account":hex64,"balance":decimal};
  ; "" on error, NEVER zero: a sequencer that cannot be reached must not read
  ; as "broke". There is no exists flag, because for native an absent account
  ; and a zero-balance one are the same answer.
  method get_native_balance(account_id: tstr) -> tstr

  ; Membership PDA read + lifecycle state derived from the on-chain CLOCK_50
  ; timestamp (never local time). {"registered":false} when the PDA is absent
  ; or emptied (erase/slash); otherwise {"clock_timestamp":N,
  ; "grace_period_duration":N,"grace_period_start_timestamp":N,
  ; "leaf_index"?:N,"rate_limit":N,"registered":true,
  ; "state":"active"|"grace_period"|"expired"}; leaf_index (since 7.0.0) when
  ; this module sent the registration — the claim of the send that landed.
  ; "" on error (including clock fetch failure). clock_timestamp and
  ; grace_period_start_timestamp are MILLISECONDS (CLOCK_50);
  ; grace_period_duration is SECONDS.
  method get_membership(config_account_id: tstr, id_commitment_hex: tstr) -> tstr

  ; Registry-declared registration bounds: the compile-time rate-limit range
  ; plus ConfigState capacity/pricing/duration fields read by offset.
  ; price_per_unit is a decimal STRING (u128 exceeds JSON number precision)
  ; and is denominated in NATIVE balance. {"active_duration":N,
  ; "current_total_rate_limit":N,"grace_period_duration":N,"max_rate_limit":600,
  ; "max_total_rate_limit":N,"min_rate_limit":100,"price_per_unit":"<decimal>",
  ; "total_registrations":N}; "" on error. active_duration and
  ; grace_period_duration are SECONDS.
  method get_registry_bounds(config_account_id: tstr) -> tstr

  ; Whether the lez_core wallet is open and usable to this module, and which
  ; account it pays with:
  ; {"detail":s,"network":s,"payer":hex64,"ready":b,
  ;  "state":"pending"|"ready"|"failed"}.
  ; `network` (since 4.1.0) is the network the home is recorded as bound to,
  ; "" while unbound or when the home was configured by its operator.
  ; Never fails and never touches the chain — `payer` is the last pick (the
  ; best-funded account, or the one published for funding when none is), so
  ; callers poll this as a liveness probe. Fund that account, or any account
  ; in the wallet: get_native_balance("") re-picks and reports the result.
  ; Branch on `state`, not on `ready`: the distinction that matters is
  ; retry-or-give-up. "pending" is bring-up still in flight (asking lez_core
  ; for its dir, opening the wallet, picking a payer) and worth waiting on;
  ; "failed" will not resolve by waiting (lez_core open on another chain,
  ; LEZ_RLN_PAYER not in the wallet), and
  ; `detail` says why. Every chain-facing method answers "" until "ready".
  ; Since 4.1.0 an unconfigured home is "pending" with the detail "no network
  ; selected — no wallet_config.json, LEZ_RLN_SEQUENCER unset;
  ; liblogos_rln_module.start selects one from its registry ids" until
  ; use_network binds it.
  method wallet_status() -> tstr

  ; Select the network this module's wallet talks to by the CAIP-2 reference
  ; of a `logos` registry id (lowercased), or check it against the one already
  ; chosen. Never touches the chain.
  ; {"accepted":b,"detail":s,"network":s,"retry":b,
  ;  "source":"table"|"env"|"operator"|""}.
  ; - home not resolved yet (on_context_ready pending): accepted:false,
  ;   retry:true — ask again.
  ; - home unconfigured: a reference in the built-in table writes
  ;   wallet_config.json + network.json, starts bring-up, and is accepted
  ;   (source "table"); an unknown one is refused, listing the known ones.
  ; - home bound to a recorded network: accepted for that reference, refused
  ;   for any other (a home is never re-pointed).
  ; - home configured by its operator (no network.json): accepted for any
  ;   reference, source "operator" — the network is not checked.
  ; Refusals are final (retry:false); `network` is the bound network on
  ; refusal, the accepted one otherwise. Chain-facing methods also refuse a
  ; config account the table places on a network other than the bound one.
  method use_network(reference: tstr) -> tstr

  ; Since 4.2.0. The head fee market of the sequencer this module's wallet is
  ; configured with, read from that sequencer's JSON-RPC getFeeState: its
  ; `result` object passed through, e.g. {"base_fee_exec":8,
  ; "base_fee_stor":8,"height":N,"max_gas_exec":10000000,
  ; "max_gas_stor":1000000,"next_base_fee_exec_ceiling":9,
  ; "next_base_fee_exec_floor":8,"next_base_fee_stor_ceiling":9,
  ; "next_base_fee_stor_floor":8}. The next_* pair bounds the base fee of the
  ; next block (floor: an empty block, ceiling: a full one).
  ; "" until a network is selected, and on any transport or parse error. Needs
  ; the wallet's network, not the wallet: it answers during bring-up. http
  ; and https sequencers are both read. Bounded by a 5s connect + 10s read
  ; timeout.
  method get_fee_state() -> tstr

  ; Whether a registry is usable here, and if not, why — so a caller can say
  ; "not deployed on this chain" instead of failing on its first read.
  ; {"status":s,"detail":s?,"registration_program":hex64?,"sequencer":s?,
  ; "chain_head":N?}. status: "ok" | "not_deployed" (the config account holds
  ; no program state: a reset network, or a registry that never existed
  ; there) | "wrong_generation" (a config from another program version) |
  ; "unexpected_layout" | "network_conflict" (the table places it on another
  ; network than the wallet's) | "unreachable" (the sequencer gave no usable
  ; answer) | "invalid" (not an account id). chain_head is the sequencer's last
  ; block id: a low one next to "not_deployed" points at a reset.
  method check_registry(config_account_id: tstr) -> tstr

}
